**F-C01 — Bound source transformation.** Use the source-patchset contract F-P01–F-P06 and L-F01–L-F07. The root is the existing json-services-section package; only scripts/canonical-json.mjs (original SHA 21c4b0fb8d1ce06e7e95f0b4e40bde25613b4392a80bb40a36749f7375d4b1b3) and scripts/is-json-value.mjs (original SHA f154946c4578044ae978132103ad297826ea196ede2ec583ddd800e129cc25b7) may be edited. Preserve module exports, default exports, CLI entrypoints, input/output schemas and all unrelated source behavior. No new imports, dependencies, files or package exports. The generated patchset carries exact original hashes and unique substring replacements. The source bytes are migration evidence for existing public semantics, not authority to preserve stack overflow.

**F-C02 — Iterative canonical projection.** Replace recursive descent over runtime values with explicit frames. Preserve finite-number admission and negative-zero normalization, Unicode scalar validation, UTF-16 ordinal object-key ordering, array order, plain-object/descriptor restrictions, cycle refusal and acceptance of shared acyclic subtrees. Preserve exact canonical text, byteLength and deeply frozen detached value snapshots. Preserve code/path/message for existing shallow refusals where input violates the same first condition. Keep the exact envelope constants and defaults; honor each supplied envelope dimension independently with its existing unit, threshold and diagnostic. Root container depth is zero: a container at depth >= maxDepth refuses; primitive leaves do not consume an additional container depth. Each runtime node occurrence is charged, including repeated shared values; key bytes are charged separately. Never invoke getters or toJSON during canonical projection. Check array descriptors without quadratic rescanning of the full key set per index. Build canonical output as a linear token sequence and join once. Keep linked diagnostic path segments; expand a full path only when throwing. Frozen child values are attached to parents without recursively freezing or reserializing descendants. Unbounded defaults remain unbounded policies, not call-stack limits.

**F-C03 — Iterative strict text admission.** Replace recursive container descent in the existing strict parser with explicit frames and grammar states. Keep strict whitespace/token/number rules, fatal malformed UTF-8 rejection, duplicate decoded object-key detection, Unicode surrogate handling, safe own properties including __proto__, exact resource-limit thresholds and diagnostic locations. JSON.parse may decode an individual already isolated JSON string; do not replace complete-document admission with JSON.parse, which loses duplicate-key evidence. Reject trailing commas, missing separators/values and trailing input. Preserve the parsing order of invalid conditions and existing messages for shallow cases. Input bytes are charged before parsing; canonical bytes may differ from source bytes and retain their independent bound. Do not recurse indirectly through projection or full-document stringification. Complete text admission still returns the canonical frozen snapshot through the one shared projection.

